{
  "method": "A regularized logistic model fits prior completed US observations using chart features, stock-local historical score, longer returns and fixed interactions. Each year select among score thresholds using only previous-rule bearish calls in the prior two years whose exits completed before test year; require 20 calls, 6 months, 5 symbols, >=51% hit and >=1 percentage point improvement over previous-rule validation calls, otherwise abstain. Test calls must also pass the previous momentum/contrarian local rule. Model fit outcomes end strictly before validation starts. Same 2020-2026 eligible sample and replay as prior US rule; PARA excluded from observations, market gate, and peer ranks. First monthly close versus first close on or after 3 calendar months, at most 10 days late; ties are misses.",
  "limitations": [
    "Exploratory after extensive repeated inspection, not an untouched or prospective test; model and threshold search create selection bias not included in intervals.",
    "Selected current listings omit many delisted stocks; history may be revised or have ticker identity/corporate action errors. PARA exclusion was chosen after inspection. Pending and missing outcomes are excluded.",
    "Peer previous local dates do not guarantee availability at the signal time. Overlapping calls and shared shocks are correlated; no costs, dividends, taxes, slippage or executable same-close entry. No app deployment."
  ],
